### Add a prefix with `$before` and a suffix with `$after`

Use these directives when each direct child needs the same prefix or suffix.
Either works alone. Here each child gets a pair of list-item tags.

[codeblock, $code "moth":
    items #= [$before "<li>", $after "</li>":[$slot]]
    steps = [items:[:Build][:Test]]
]

The result contains two items, `<li>Build</li><li>Test</li>`. The bracket
around each word gives the parent two children to wrap.

### Skip one wrapper with `$fresh`

Put `$fresh` on the child that should skip its immediate parent's prefix
and suffix. A child that supplies its own list-item markup can use it to
avoid a second pair of tags.

[codeblock, $code "moth":
    steps = [items:[:Build][$fresh:<li class="current">Test</li>]]
]

Only the first child gets the usual tags. The second keeps its own class.
